  "topsides": "#2b2a27",
  "expedition": true,
  "notes": "A Jamaica-built sloop of the kind the rovers liked about 1715: red cedar, sharp, a mast raked well aft, a very long boom and bowsprit. About 60 ft on deck, 20 ft beam, 100 tons. Every figure is typical of the type as I remember it described, not any one vessel, and none was checked. The polar is a judgement: they were the fastest craft in the Indies, good for eleven knots reaching in a fresh trade wind, and would lie five points from the wind. The sim has one mainsail and one headsail: the square topsail and the flying squaresail such sloops set before the wind are not drawn, and their drive is counted in the polar, which is why she runs nearly as fast as she reaches. Rigging shot away is modelled by lowering the 'drive' of the sail plans on the session's own copy of this file.",
